---
title: Life is interesting
description: I don't know whether life has meaning. Lately I'm more interested in why we keep asking.
date: 2026-06-22
readingTime: 2 min read
tags:
  - philosophy
  - consciousness
  - meaning
---

Life is interesting.

I don't know if it has meaning or if we're just making it up as we go, I don't know if the universe is absurd or if we're simply too small to understand it. Most people seem desperate to pick a side, I never found that convincing.

What interests me is the experience itself.

Suffering is interesting, happiness is interesting, love is interesting. The fact that I can sit here and feel sad, then step outside of that sadness and think about it, that's interesting too. Even depression is interesting, not because it's good, not because I enjoy it, but because it exists at all.

A conscious mind is a strange thing, it can suffer and watch itself suffer at the same time, it can know something is irrational and still feel it, it can create meaning, destroy it, then spend years wondering whether it was ever there in the first place.

People ask whether life is meaningful, I think the more interesting question is why we're asking. Why do we care so much? Why does the possibility of meaninglessness bother us? Why do we keep searching?

Maybe life has meaning, maybe it doesn't, I don't know.

What I do know is that every time I think I've understood something, another question appears behind it, every answer creates two more questions, every person turns out more complicated than they first seemed, every emotion has layers under it.

For me that's enough, not because I found the answer, because I haven't.

The search is the interesting part, whether meaning exists is almost secondary.
